I've done a few small patches that alter the behaviour of certain
magical (and non-magical) items when they're cursed/blessed.

This first patch has already been available for some time. It arose
from my opinion that a curse on a wand doesn't offer enough of a
disincentive to using it. It makes it so that, in addition to the 1%
exploding chance, cursed directional wands have a 10% chance of
backfiring (zapping you instead of your desired direction.)
<<http://www.greyfire.org/~l/c-zap.diff>>

This patch makes it so that playing a cursed bugle teleports all of the
soldiers on a level to you. The logic behind this one is the same as
for a blessed eucalyptus leaf summoning pets, only reversed.
<<http://www.greyfire.org/~l/c-bugle.diff>>

This patch makes it so that playing a cursed whistle while in a vault
summons the vault guard immediately - on the basis that guards'
whistles are always "shrill" and a cursed whistle makes a shrill sound.
<<http://www.greyfire.org/~l/c-whistle.diff>>

This patch makes it so that blessed dunce caps and helms of opposite
alignment do not automatically curse themselves when they're worn. This
is probably the most utilitarian of the patches here.
<<http://www.greyfire.org/~l/c-dunce.diff>>

This patch makes it so that blessed loadstones do not automatically
curse themselves, and makes a thrown loadstone do d25 damage instead of
d3 damage. Not really that useful, I must admit, but it follows the
logic of the previous patch.
<<http://www.greyfire.org/~l/c-loadstone.diff>>



